  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response to communities affected by flooding in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1,980 households have improved knowledged on protection (GbV and PSEA) and DRR (earthquake measures)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">300 households that lost their gardens have recieved seeds, able to earn a fairly rapid income after the July harvest given that this is a short-cycle crop; gauranteeing a significant food source</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">710  households have improved hygiene conditions and are better able to fight against water-bourne diseases</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">710 households are able to meet their food needs for 1 month.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will respond to most of the urgent needs highlighted by the DGPC (shelter, drinking water, hygiene, and food security.), and the PAHO (awareness and prevention of diarrheal diseases, including cholera, sanitation/health kits for women in temporary shelters), within two of the worst affected areas, Petit-Go&#xE2;ve, in L&#xE9;og&#xE2;ne, in the Ouest department and Petit Trou des Nippes and Plaisance du Sud in the Nippes Department.</narrative>
  </description>
